          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1770641618213,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let's say, df1 data size is bigger than the storage memory. Then,\nExecutor will try to store as much data as it can in the storage memory,\nand rest of the data will be either RECOMPUTED or SPILLED to disk.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let's say, df1 data size is bigger than the storage memory. Then,\nExecutor will try to store as much data as it can in the storage memory,\nand rest of the data will be either RECOMPUTED or SPILLED to disk.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
