    {
      "id": "M3NtOz3H2C0GZ00U_ie4f",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3034.040632295463,
      "y": 189463.95769827807,
      "width": 1977.5828857421875,
      "height": 5056.766172250109,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#e9ecef",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c2gB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1048109707,
      "version": 1768,
      "versionNonce": 1169085899,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1771616070834,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\nIn-Memory Columnar Storage\n\n- spark.sql.inMemoryColumnarStorage.compressed: \n        When set to true, Spark SQL automatically selects a compression codec for each column based on data statistics.\n\n- spark.sql.inMemoryColumnarStorage.batchSize: \n        Controls the size of batches for columnar caching to improve memory utilization, though large sizes risk out-of-memory errors.\n\n\nFile-Based Source Tuning\n\n\n- spark.sql.files.maxPartitionBytes:\n        Sets the maximum number of bytes to pack into a single partition when reading file-based sources like Parquet, JSON, and ORC.\n\n- spark.sql.files.openCostInBytes: \n        Estimates the cost to open a file in bytes to help Spark decide how to pack multiple small files into a single partition.\n\n- spark.sql.files.minPartitionNum: \n        Provides a suggested minimum number of split file partitions for file-based sources.\n\n- spark.sql.files.maxPartitionNum: \n        Provides a suggested maximum number of split file partitions, triggering Spark to rescale partitions if the initial number is too high.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.parallelPartitionDiscovery.threshold: \n        Configures the threshold of input paths required to enable parallel file listing via a distributed Spark job.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.parallelPartitionDiscovery.parallelism: \n        Configures the maximum parallelism used when listing job input paths.\n\n\nShuffle and Join Configuration\n\n\n- spark.sql.shuffle.partitions: \n        Configures the number of partitions to use when shuffling data for joins or aggregations.\n\n- spark.sql.autoBroadcastJoinThreshold: \n        Configures the maximum size in bytes for a table to be broadcast to all worker nodes during a join; set to -1 to disable.\n\n- spark.sql.broadcastTimeout: \n        Sets the timeout in seconds for the wait time during broadcast joins.\n\n\nAdaptive Query Execution (AQE)\n\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.enabled: \n        The umbrella configuration to enable or disable Adaptive Query Execution.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.advisoryPartitionSizeInBytes : \n        The target size of shuffle partitions during adaptive optimizations like coalescing or splitting skewed partitions.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.enabled: \n        When enabled with AQE, Spark will coalesce small contiguous shuffle partitions to avoid excessive small tasks.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.parallelismFirst: \n        When true, Spark ignores the advisory partition size to respect a minimum partition size and maximize parallelism.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.minPartitionSize: \n        Defines the minimum size of shuffle partitions after coalescing has occurred.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.initialPartitionNum: \n        Sets the initial number of shuffle partitions before coalescing begins.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.optimizeSkewsInRebalancePartitions.enabled: \n        Enables the optimization and splitting of skewed shuffle partitions during rebalance operations.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.rebalancePartitionsSmallPartitionFactor: \n        A factor used to determine if a partition is small enough to be merged during a splitting operation.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.autoBroadcastJoinThreshold: \n        Configures the maximum table size for broadcasting specifically within the AQE framework.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.localShuffleReader.enabled: \n        Allows Spark to use a local shuffle reader when shuffle partitioning is not strictly required.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.maxShuffledHashJoinLocalMapThreshold: \n        Configures the maximum size per partition allowed to build a local hash map to prefer shuffled hash joins over sort-merge joins.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.skewJoin.enabled: \n        Enables dynamic handling of data skew in sort-merge joins by splitting skewed partitions into evenly sized tasks.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.skewJoin.skewedPartitionFactor: \n        A multiplier used with the median partition size to identify if a partition is skewed.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.skewJoin.skewedPartitionThresholdInBytes: \n        The minimum byte size a partition must exceed to be considered skewed.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.forceOptimizeSkewedJoin: \n        Forces the optimization of skewed joins even if it necessitates an extra shuffle.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.optimizer.excludedRules: \n        Allows users to specify a comma-separated list of optimizer rules to disable within AQE.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.customCostEvaluatorClass: \n        Defines a custom class for cost evaluation during adaptive execution.\n\n\nStorage Partition Join \n\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.enabled: \n        Enables shuffle elimination by leveraging partitioning reported by compatible V2 data sources.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.pushPartValues.enabled: \n        Attempts to eliminate shuffles when one join side has missing partition values from the other.\n\n- spark.sql.requireAllClusterKeysForCoPartition: \n        Requires join or MERGE keys to match the partition keys exactly to eliminate a shuffle.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.partiallyClusteredDistribution.enabled: \n        Enables skew optimizations for V2 bucketing by partially clustering one side of a join.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.allowJoinKeysSubsetOfPartitionKeys.enabled: \n        Attempts to avoid shuffles even if join conditions do not include every partition column.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.allowCompatibleTransforms.enabled: \n        Attempts to avoid shuffles if partition transforms are compatible but not identical.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.shuffle.enabled: \n        Attempts to avoid shuffle on one side by recognizing the V2 data source partitioning on the other side.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 32.3633035024007,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\nIn-Memory Columnar Storage\n\n- spark.sql.inMemoryColumnarStorage.compressed: \n        When set to true, Spark SQL automatically selects a compression codec for each column based on data statistics.\n\n- spark.sql.inMemoryColumnarStorage.batchSize: \n        Controls the size of batches for columnar caching to improve memory utilization, though large sizes risk out-of-memory errors.\n\n\nFile-Based Source Tuning\n\n\n- spark.sql.files.maxPartitionBytes:\n        Sets the maximum number of bytes to pack into a single partition when reading file-based sources like Parquet, JSON, and ORC.\n\n- spark.sql.files.openCostInBytes: \n        Estimates the cost to open a file in bytes to help Spark decide how to pack multiple small files into a single partition.\n\n- spark.sql.files.minPartitionNum: \n        Provides a suggested minimum number of split file partitions for file-based sources.\n\n- spark.sql.files.maxPartitionNum: \n        Provides a suggested maximum number of split file partitions, triggering Spark to rescale partitions if the initial number is too high.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.parallelPartitionDiscovery.threshold: \n        Configures the threshold of input paths required to enable parallel file listing via a distributed Spark job.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.parallelPartitionDiscovery.parallelism: \n        Configures the maximum parallelism used when listing job input paths.\n\n\nShuffle and Join Configuration\n\n\n- spark.sql.shuffle.partitions: \n        Configures the number of partitions to use when shuffling data for joins or aggregations.\n\n- spark.sql.autoBroadcastJoinThreshold: \n        Configures the maximum size in bytes for a table to be broadcast to all worker nodes during a join; set to -1 to disable.\n\n- spark.sql.broadcastTimeout: \n        Sets the timeout in seconds for the wait time during broadcast joins.\n\n\nAdaptive Query Execution (AQE)\n\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.enabled: \n        The umbrella configuration to enable or disable Adaptive Query Execution.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.advisoryPartitionSizeInBytes : \n        The target size of shuffle partitions during adaptive optimizations like coalescing or splitting skewed partitions.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.enabled: \n        When enabled with AQE, Spark will coalesce small contiguous shuffle partitions to avoid excessive small tasks.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.parallelismFirst: \n        When true, Spark ignores the advisory partition size to respect a minimum partition size and maximize parallelism.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.minPartitionSize: \n        Defines the minimum size of shuffle partitions after coalescing has occurred.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.initialPartitionNum: \n        Sets the initial number of shuffle partitions before coalescing begins.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.optimizeSkewsInRebalancePartitions.enabled: \n        Enables the optimization and splitting of skewed shuffle partitions during rebalance operations.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.rebalancePartitionsSmallPartitionFactor: \n        A factor used to determine if a partition is small enough to be merged during a splitting operation.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.autoBroadcastJoinThreshold: \n        Configures the maximum table size for broadcasting specifically within the AQE framework.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.localShuffleReader.enabled: \n        Allows Spark to use a local shuffle reader when shuffle partitioning is not strictly required.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.maxShuffledHashJoinLocalMapThreshold: \n        Configures the maximum size per partition allowed to build a local hash map to prefer shuffled hash joins over sort-merge joins.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.skewJoin.enabled: \n        Enables dynamic handling of data skew in sort-merge joins by splitting skewed partitions into evenly sized tasks.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.skewJoin.skewedPartitionFactor: \n        A multiplier used with the median partition size to identify if a partition is skewed.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.skewJoin.skewedPartitionThresholdInBytes: \n        The minimum byte size a partition must exceed to be considered skewed.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.forceOptimizeSkewedJoin: \n        Forces the optimization of skewed joins even if it necessitates an extra shuffle.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.optimizer.excludedRules: \n        Allows users to specify a comma-separated list of optimizer rules to disable within AQE.\n\n- spark.sql.adaptive.customCostEvaluatorClass: \n        Defines a custom class for cost evaluation during adaptive execution.\n\n\nStorage Partition Join \n\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.enabled: \n        Enables shuffle elimination by leveraging partitioning reported by compatible V2 data sources.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.pushPartValues.enabled: \n        Attempts to eliminate shuffles when one join side has missing partition values from the other.\n\n- spark.sql.requireAllClusterKeysForCoPartition: \n        Requires join or MERGE keys to match the partition keys exactly to eliminate a shuffle.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.partiallyClusteredDistribution.enabled: \n        Enables skew optimizations for V2 bucketing by partially clustering one side of a join.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.allowJoinKeysSubsetOfPartitionKeys.enabled: \n        Attempts to avoid shuffles even if join conditions do not include every partition column.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.allowCompatibleTransforms.enabled: \n        Attempts to avoid shuffles if partition transforms are compatible but not identical.\n\n- spark.sql.sources.v2.bucketing.shuffle.enabled: \n        Attempts to avoid shuffle on one side by recognizing the V2 data source partitioning on the other side.\n\n",
